    (also at https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)

at your option.

WHY BOTH. This is the Rust ecosystem's convention and it exists because the two licences cover
different worries. MIT is short and universally understood. Apache-2.0 adds an explicit patent
grant and a patent-retaliation clause, which some organisations require before they will take a
dependency. Offering both means neither preference blocks adoption.

CONTRIBUTIONS. Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for inclusion
in this work — as defined in the Apache-2.0 licence — shall be dual-licensed as above, with no
additional terms or conditions. Inbound equals outbound; there is no CLA.

THIRD-PARTY CODE. This repository builds against, and ships a binary linked with, code under other
licences — notably godot-rust (gdext) under MPL-2.0. See THIRD_PARTY.md for the full inventory and
for why the MPL dependency does not change your obligations as a user of OrbitNet.
